{% set local_problem %}
<p>Guntersville gutters fill up fast. Pine needles accumulate year-round. Hardwood leaves fall heavily in autumn. The lake environment adds organic debris that blows onto roofs and into gutters. Without regular cleaning, clogs develop quickly.</p>

<p>Near the lake, clogged gutters are more than an inconvenience — they accelerate damage. Standing water in gutters promotes corrosion. Overflow keeps fascia boards constantly damp, encouraging rot. Water pooling at foundations eventually finds its way into basements and crawlspaces.</p>

<p>The humid environment means problems develop faster here than in drier areas. A gutter clog that might be minor elsewhere can cause significant damage at a lake home, especially if it goes unnoticed on a vacation property.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our cleaning service is designed for Guntersville's demanding environment. We hand-remove all debris from gutters — not just blow it onto your lawn. We flush every downspout to ensure they're flowing freely.</p>

<p>Critically, we inspect your entire gutter system for damage while we're up there. Lake humidity causes corrosion, loose hangers, and wood rot that might not be visible from the ground. Catching these problems early prevents expensive repairs later.</p>

<p>For vacation property owners, we can coordinate with your property manager, schedule around rental bookings, and provide photo documentation of completed work and any issues found.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters on Lake Guntersville properties for over 20 years. We understand the environment, the challenges of steep lakefront lots, and the needs of vacation rental owners.</p>

<p>We show up when scheduled, do thorough work, and communicate clearly about what we find. That reliability matters when you're managing a property from a distance.</p>
{% endset %}
